Z||000003||ChadMan||01-29-2001||10:53 AM||||These terms come from Corbin's "Fiero Spotter's Guide" -- at least, I'd never heard or read "STD I" and STD II" until I bought the Spotter's Guide.  At any rate...<P>STD I = Standard I = 1984-86 Coupe + 85 SE<BR>STD II = Standard II = 1987-88 Coupe + 88 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||01-29-2001||11:54 AM||||stimpy, don't worry about any of that stuff - they have shots and pills for that now........(and, yes, it refers to the type of fascia (or "bumper cover")||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierogt88||01-29-2001||02:04 PM||||Stimpy, I too have a problem with the lingo...<P>I need to know what TDC is and how it relates to PUSHROD concerning 3.4 engines...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||01-29-2001||02:31 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierogt88:<BR><B>Stimpy, I too have a problem with the lingo...<P>I need to know what TDC is and how it relates to PUSHROD concerning 3.4 engines...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Pushrod = Camshaft in engine block. Uses lifters to push rods to push rocker arms. They in turn open the valve.<P>TDC = "Twin Dual Cam" There are 2 cams in each head of the engine. (24-valves and 4 camshafts) It goes cam to lifter to valve.<P>OHC = "Over Head Cam". Camshaft is located in the head of a inline engine.<P>DOHC = "Dual Over Head Cam" Usually A "V" type engine (V-6 or V-8) that has one camshaft in each head. OR an in-line engine can use 2 cams in the head also. These are the 16-valve 4-cylinder engines<BR>Basically its 1 cam for 2-valves per cylinder, and usually 2 cams for 4-valve's per cylinder.<P>Hope this helps. <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Greg Piet||01-29-2001||02:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierogt88:<BR><B>I need to know what TDC is and how it relates to PUSHROD concerning 3.4 engines...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Geez and I always thought TDC was top dead center.||||reg||1
Z||000008||ray b||01-29-2001||05:46 PM||||oreif no one cam per head=sohc can be one in each head in v6 0r v8 like new ford.<BR>dohc= 2per head not motor total can be dohc-v6 with 4 cams, still dohc if only 2 valve and some 4 valve with only one cam rare .<BR>allso some with 3valve honda and 5valve bikes and race motors. ray ||||reg||1
