Z||000023||ray b||01-31-2001||09:01 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by Oreif:<BR>[B]  HUH?<BR>There is not a DOHC engine (for cars) that has 2 valves per cylinder and 2 cams in the head.  This is a car forum not a bike/motorcycle forum.]<BR> ever see a strait 6 jag 2 valves per cyl with 2 cams 1947 till 80's only one of many cars to use this set up. porsche dohc flat 4 had 4 cams with 2 valves, most older dohc cars only had 2 valves. like aston martin or ferrari before quatro valve.<BR>twin dual cam tdc is G M only V6 sales name not used on N* or vett zr motors.<BR>yamaha gp f1 motor used 5 valves in race CAR.<BR>   ray<P><BR>||||reg||1
